# Security and access control

Read `config/WebSecurityConfig.java`, the relevant controller, and the Keycloak configuration before making security changes.

## Current verified state

- Spring Security and OAuth2 Resource Server JWT support are configured.
- Keycloak login and current-user identity endpoints exist under `auth/` and call infrastructure services.
- `WebSecurityConfig` currently ends authorization with `.anyRequest().permitAll()`. As a result, the API is not currently protected by authentication even though JWT support is configured.
- Method-security support is enabled, but the current code does not define role/scope annotations on controllers or services.
- There is no implemented business-manager/branch-manager authorization model in this repository.

Do not claim that an endpoint is protected merely because Keycloak, JWT, or method security is present. Do not transplant user/business/branch scopes or role rules from another project. If asked to secure an endpoint, first establish the intended actors and ownership rules with the existing pet-clinic domain, then enforce them server-side and add suitable tests.

Never trust a request-supplied owner, vet, clinic, pet, or other resource UUID as proof of authorization. Once authorization is implemented, validate that the authenticated actor is permitted to access the referenced records.

Treat credentials in profile YAML as sensitive. Do not print, copy, or commit them. Prefer environment-backed secrets when introducing or changing configuration.
